{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310807,"nonce":"9fsYxNctBA1L4Mq4rJqj0LGkwIA=","title":"Q4_K_M SDOT 4-way partial accumulator unroll. +1.42% short-form, +6.95% long-form (31.14 → 33.3 tok/s on user's Voronoi 600-tok prompt). ...","message":"`dot_q4_k_q8` and `dot_q4_k_q8_kblock` in `runtime/src/quant.rs` previously serialized a scalar `sum_term1 += sub_scale * sdot` and `sum_term2 += sub_min * bsum` chain across 4 loop iterations. M1 Pro's wide OoO scheduler can't hide that — each iteration's accumulate depends on the prior one.\n\nReplaced single accumulators with `[f32; 4]` per-p partials, folded via balanced pair-wise tree at the end:\n\n```rust\np1[p] = sub_scale_lo * lo_sdot + sub_scale_hi * hi_sdot;\np2[p] = sub_min_lo * bsum_lo32 as f32 + sub_min_hi * bsum_hi32 as f32;\n...\nlet s1 = (p1[0] + p1[1]) + (p1[2] + p1[3]);\nlet s2 = (p2[0] + p2[1]) + (p2[2] + p2[3]);\nx.d * (s1 - s2)\n```\n\nSame f32 operations, same ULP floor; only the reduction tree shape changes. Paris MATCH byte-identical.\n\n\n**In-iteration SDOT acc split** — instead of the existing serial `acc = vdotq_s32(acc, a, b); acc = vdotq_s32(acc, c, d);` chain, split into two independent partials folded by `vaddq_s32`. Compiles fine but **SIGSEGVs `matmul_qt_t_f32_matches_dequant_then_matmul_t`** unit test. Root cause not investigated. The partial-only path is sufficient.\n\n\nPaired A/B (N=10, AC power, stash-rebuild discipline), Paris-history 64-tok:\n- WITH UNROLL: median 21.551 tok/s (mean 21.503, stdev 0.120)\n- BASELINE:    median 21.250 tok/s (mean 21.262, stdev 0.072)\n- **+1.42% median win**\n- Cross-pairs sign test: WITH \u003e BASE in 94/100 (p \u003c 0.001)\n\nLong-form (Voronoi 600-tok, ctx=4096), 3-run mean: **33.3 tok/s**\n- vs prior post-JIT-fix baseline (user-reported): **31.14 tok/s**\n- **+6.95% on long-form**\n\nThe bigger long-form delta is consistent with matmul share growing with context length: at decode-time `vec_dot_q4_K_q8_K` is called once per (n_row, K-block) pair, and Llama 3.2 1B with hidden=2048 / vocab=128256 hits ~140k super-blocks per token. Each super-block was paying ~4 dependent adds on the critical path.\n\n\nThe earlier Q4_K_M 2-row tile attempt washed out at +0.01% pre-JIT-fix (`bugs_q4km_sdot_tile_no_win.md`). Different axis (cross-row vs cross-iteration), but same noise-floor problem: the 655d7ac JIT fix unblocked the optimizer pipeline, which removed trap-stub pollution that was masking small per-call wins. Now per-call gains compound visibly.\n\nThis suggests the workflow's earlier \"rejected\" candidates — Cranelift FMA fusion, K/V layout tweaks, etc. — should ALL be re-evaluated post-JIT-fix. The noise floor was higher than the win was.\n\n\n- [[bugs-w0020-value-map-miss-cross-loop]] — the JIT fix that unblocked this win.\n- [[bugs-q4km-sdot-tile-no-win]] — same kernel, earlier attempt that washed out pre-JIT-fix.\n- [[bugs-q6k-sdot-no-win]] — Q6_K SDOT washed out under the same disciplined methodology; worth re-running post-JIT-fix.\n- [[bugs-sys-getenv-in-ctor-residual]] — discovered during the RoPE fused attempt that aborted this session.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `perf_q4km_sdot_4way_unroll` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}